<div class="guide-styles" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">Welcome to Wowhead's Phase 4 Best in Slot Gear list for Balance Druid DPS in Wrath of the Lich King Classic. Gear in this guide is primarily obtained from Icecrown Citadel. This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from raids, dungeons, PvP, professions, Bind on Equip drops, and reputations.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot">Best in Slot Gear for Balance Druid DPS Phase 4</h2>In phase 4, Balance will maintain all soft caps, and we will continue to gear in a "balanced," (heh) way with haste and crit. You should always aim to meet the required Hit rating. If you are fully talented into <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=33596/balance-of-power">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_druid_balanceofpower.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Balance of Power</span></a> and <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=33602/improved-faerie-fire">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_faeriefire.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Improved Faerie Fire</span></a>, you only need 10% Hit from gear (263 rating) to reach the hit cap requirement for a boss fight. Furthermore, if you play for the Alliance, Draenei provide <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=28878/heroic-presence">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_21.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Heroic Presence</span></a> to their party members, bringing your required Hit to 9% (236 rating).<br/>
<br/>As always, crit continues to be a very strong stat for Balance. In Phase 4 we will maintain a mana neutral to mana positive state, however, there is plenty of trash in ICC and mana could pose an issue while clearing to a boss.<br/>
<br/>Gear progression for Phase 4 should be 4pc Tier 9 &gt; 2pc Tier 10 + 2pc Tier 9 (replacing 245 before 258) &gt; 4pc T10 &gt; Idol.<br/>
<br/>2pc Tier 10 provides us with a damage boost whenever we gain <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=16870/clearcasting">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_manaburn.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Clearcasting</span></a> from <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=16864/omen-of-clarity">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_crystalball.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Omen of Clarity</span></a>. The 4pc bonus provides us with <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=71023/languish">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_naturetouchdecay.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Languish</span></a>, a dot that is applied when <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=48461/wrath">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_abolishmagic.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Wrath</span></a> or <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=48465/starfire">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_arcane_starfire.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Starfire</span></a> crit and works exactly like <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=12848/ignite">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_fire_incinerate.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Ignite</span></a> at reduced value.<br/>
<br/>There are two sets listed below, one assumes horde while the other assumes Alliance WITH <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=6562/heroic-presence">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_21.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Heroic Presence</span></a>. These sets also assume you have access to Engineering and Tailoring, the former being highly recommended. For more information on other options for individual slots, read the sections below.<br/>
<br/>The talents and glyphs selected in the BiS planners below contain a spec that is intended for overall damage including trash. Please see the Talents and Glyphs guide for a single target focused alternative.<br/>
<br/>
<b>
<ins>Horde note:</ins></b> <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=51872/ether-soaked-bracers">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_bracer_44.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Ether-Soaked Bracers</span></a> can in some gear setups and situations out dps <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50651/the-ladys-brittle-bracers">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_bracer_44.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">The Lady's Brittle Bracers</span></a>. In most cases during gearing, they can be interchangeable.<br/>
